:: Home_Bathroom_Wash [nobr]
<<HUD>>

<<ImagePlaceholder "Male Marcus, bathroom mirror, tired, stubble, freckles" "portrait" "assets/characters/mc-male/mirror-morning.png">>

<div class="prose-block">

<p>I turn on the shower. Cold, obviously. I called the utility company earlier with a voice full of that specific brand of dignity people scraping the bottom learn to perform. &quot;I&apos;ll have it by the fifteenth.&quot; I won&apos;t have it by the fifteenth.</p>

<p>I splash cold water on my face and look in the mirror.</p>

<p>Angular jaw with patches of stubble I can&apos;t quite grow into a full beard. Hazel-green eyes set in slightly downturned corners that make me look perpetually tired, which is fair, since I actually am perpetually tired. Dark circles like bruises under both eyes. Cheekbones too prominent because my face is too thin because I don&apos;t eat enough because food costs money I don&apos;t have.</p>

<p>Dark brown hair, wavy and overgrown past my ears, brushing my collar, because a haircut costs twenty dollars and twenty dollars is four meals.</p>

<p>Freckles scattered across my nose and upper cheeks, the one feature I&apos;ve never minded. My grandmother used to say freckles were angel kisses. She died when I was sixteen.</p>

<p>&quot;You look like shit,&quot; I tell the mirror.</p>

<p>The mirror doesn&apos;t argue with me.</p>

<p>I brush my teeth with a toothbrush that should&apos;ve been replaced two months ago, bristles splaying outward like they&apos;re trying to escape my mouth. I spit and don&apos;t look at the mirror again on my way out.</p>

</div>

